id: pm-l5bc03
title: "Exact-head review hardening: terminator-safe create mode, complete item ID conflict parsing, and public changelog integrity"
description: "Resolve all actionable exact-head review findings on PR #957 across three review rounds: preserve argument terminators and global/command option arity during item-ID normalization, reject every ambiguous item identifier form, keep command suggestions deterministic, expose exact close validation domains, prove executable aliases and tracker-scoped recovery, keep public changelog entries user-facing through canonical PM metadata, and preserve honest generator/gate evidence."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:cli","area:release","area:sdk",changelog-exclude,pr-957,regression,review-hardening
created_at: "2026-08-09T23:34:03.288Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T09:56:26.881Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#f40a3612ddfb4cf32376b325"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Create-mode and recovery policy stop at --; item addressing consumes global and command-local value flags and rejects every mixed-ID ambiguity; show --id executes through alias normalization; close-task and item-complete expose off|warn|strict validation domains; public generated changelog uses capability language; historical PM lifecycle corrections remain append-only; focused, full, coverage, static, contract, manual, and exact-head CI gates pass before closure"
parent: pm-usfg
resolution: "Aligned release preparation with canonical changelog exclusion, added bounded exact-tag changelog regeneration for unpublished immutable-tag recovery, and executable workflow guards for ordinary, recovery, and unexpected-mutation paths."
expected_result: "Every item-addressed invocation resolves one unambiguous ID through declared flag arity, create-mode policy stops at --, and generated public notes exclude internal review records."
actual_result: "Focused release contracts pass 32/32; full repository coverage passes 468 files and 7,142 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; lint, duplication, static quality, security, docs links, and tracker ratchets pass. A clean detached v2026.8.10 worktree regenerated only CHANGELOG.md plus managed-extension timestamp metadata, removed the three excluded entries, and matched reviewed main byte-for-byte."
