comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T23:34:03.288Z","harness:codex","Duplicate governance identified pm-xg60q3,but that closed item is only the prior coverage-shard ordering repair. This item is intentionally distinct because it tracks four new exact-head findings in different parser/changelog surfaces; all-status search found no canonical item for this finding set."
  "2026-08-10T00:08:49.700Z","harness:codex","Final evidence: focused parser/acceptance tests pass 9/9; full repository suite passes; exact coverage passes at statements 50,815/50,815, branches 37,177/37,177, functions 10,437/10,437, lines 49,165/49,165. ESLint has zero warnings, jscpd has zero clones, and quality:static passes all docstring, SDK boundary, replication, token/context, tracker-ratchet, import-cost, and transport-floor gates. In a fresh isolated tracker, normal --id reads succeeded, flag-interleaved positional-plus-named IDs and duplicate named IDs failed before execution, an operand --create-mode strict stayed progressive, and a real pre-terminator strict option stayed strict. pm-changelog 2026.8.7 check is unchanged with both internal entries excluded and user-facing capability entries retained."
  "2026-08-10T00:45:42.267Z","harness:codex","Review-round duplicate decision: reuse this canonical PR #957 exact-head hardening item because the new findings extend the same item-addressing parser, recovery docs, changelog governance, and gate evidence surfaces. All-status search found no more specific active owner for this combined set; pm-b84irw remains the canonical replication-gate test owner and will receive only its own waiver-specific evidence under a separate claim."
  "2026-08-10T00:45:55.566Z","harness:codex","Ownership chronology note: pm claim correctly refused the terminal item without the prohibited --force override, so the public lifecycle required reopening before a normal claim. The item is now claimed before any source, docs, tests, or further metadata implementation changes; the recovery remains append-only and no override was used."
  "2026-08-10T01:11:58.678Z","harness:codex","Second-round exact-head evidence: all five CodeRabbit findings are implemented. Recovery documentation now specifies insertion before the first --; item addressing scans the complete pre-terminator stream, consumes contract-declared option values, preserves legitimate command operands, rejects named-first mixed IDs, and has explicit copy value metadata; suggestion ties use code-point ordering; historical post-release PM chronology was remediated append-only under normal claims; the replication waiver test is linked with waiver-specific evidence. Focused SDK tests pass, pnpm typecheck passes, pnpm lint passes with zero ESLint warnings and zero jscpd clones, pnpm quality:static passes, and the full sandboxed coverage run passes 466 files / 7,111 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 (50,834 statements, 37,194 branches, 10,438 functions, 49,180 lines)."
  "2026-08-10T01:21:23.781Z","harness:codex","Exact-head CI recovery: Gates (static) correctly failed because the public copy/get flag metadata changed while tests/fixtures/contracts/full.json was stale. Regenerated the snapshot with pnpm contracts:update; pnpm contracts:check and pnpm quality:static now pass, including contract, capability, error catalog, docstring, package boundary, SDK parity, replication, token/context, tracker ratchet, surface, import-cost, and transport-floor gates."
  "2026-08-10T02:13:16.301Z","harness:codex","Third-round exact-head evidence: eight valid findings were implemented through SDK/CLI contracts, acceptance tests, canonical PM lifecycle repair, and generated release notes. Two reported functional findings were disproved against the exact head: valid --path, --author, and --output-format values after --id already resolve through the merged contract map, and the no-reason close branch intentionally emits an unscoped pm update retry; both focused tests pass. The unit primitive suite is now split by capability, normalization, terminator, and conflict behavior. Full test and coverage runs each pass 466 files / 7,114 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 (50,834 statements, 37,194 branches, 10,438 functions, 49,180 lines); all strict gates pass. A fresh isolated tracker proved show/get --id with tracker/output flags and exact off|warn|strict domains for close-task and item complete."
  "2026-08-10T09:40:33.215Z","harness:codex","Production recurrence: Auto Release run 31373926178 generated v2026.8.10 with three changelog-exclude items because prepareReleaseChangelog omitted --exclude-tag, while downstream Release run 31374837651 correctly used changelog:pm:check and failed before npm publication. Reusing this canonical changelog-integrity item; no second tag or version will be created."
  "2026-08-10T09:56:26.881Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: exact coverage 50,923/50,923 statements, 37,237/37,237 branches, 10,456/10,456 functions, and 49,265/49,265 lines across 7,142 tests. ESLint, jscpd zero clones, 100% docstrings/static quality, secret scan, docs links, tracker measurements, focused executable workflow tests, and detached-tag manual recovery all pass. The sole v2026.8.10 tag remains unchanged at f4dcfa8460d3934004e449f93bf138ceef2c535b; npm publication has not yet occurred."
learnings[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T00:08:50.099Z","harness:codex",Argument normalization must parse option arity from the same command flag contracts as Commander; fixed-position scans cannot distinguish option values from item operands once flags are interleaved.
  "2026-08-10T00:08:50.548Z","harness:codex","Public changelog exclusion is an invocation policy as well as item metadata: the generator's --exclude-tag contract must be present in both generate and check scripts."
  "2026-08-10T01:11:59.111Z","harness:codex","Option-aware item addressing is a small grammar, not a positional splice: scan the entire pre-terminator stream, consume values from the public flag contract, and model legitimate trailing operands per command before deciding that a second item ID exists."
  "2026-08-10T01:11:59.583Z","harness:codex",Deterministic agent output must not depend on host locale; score ties need explicit code-point comparison and an equality branch for duplicate command paths.
  "2026-08-10T02:13:16.696Z","harness:codex",Generated contract snapshots must be refreshed after rebuilding changed TypeScript contracts; otherwise the updater can snapshot the preceding dist artifact and the subsequent check correctly reports drift.
